# Project-specific
# Benchmark outputs. The published runs are committed: the README's results tables are
# generated from them, so a reader has to be able to see the run behind a published
# number. Those live in a subdirectory named after the LexiChunk build that produced them
# (results/lexichunk_fixed/, results/lexichunk_baseline/). Ad-hoc runs land in results/
# itself with the CLI's default filenames and are not committed, so `make
# benchmark-structural` on a developer's machine never rewrites the evidence. Rendered
# reports and caches are not committed either.
results/*
!results/*/
results/*/*
!results/*/*.json
.cache/
*.faiss
requirements.lock
scaffolder.yaml

# Internal build artifacts (agent plans, research, task tracking)
plans/
reference-docs/
research-docs/
tasks/lessons.md
tasks/gap-analysis-*.md

# Claude Code settings
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# Environment variables
.env
.env.local

